{"id":"1974-04-03-superoutbreak","name":"The 1974 Super Outbreak","region":"Thirteen states","blurb":"Thirty violent tornadoes in eighteen hours, six of them F5. Every F4 and F5 of the outbreak is here, with the tornadoes that ran alongside them.","scale":"F","tz":"America/Chicago","T0":134231400,"source":"NOAA Storm Prediction Center tornado database (1950\u20132025)","pathFidelity":"3 of 76 tracks are the surveyed centreline from NOAA's Damage Assessment Toolkit; the rest are straight lines between surveyed endpoints","torn":[{"name":"Boone, IN","ef":"EF2","start":0,"end":60,"coords":[[-86.3,40.03],[-86.2986,40.0309]],"lengthMi":0.1,"widthYd":50.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"IN","geometry":"point","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Gilmer\u2013Fannin, GA","ef":"EF2","start":12600,"end":13723,"coords":[[-84.5,34.68],[-84.32,34.85]],"lengthMi":15.6,"widthYd":200.0,"inj":5,"fat":0,"state":"GA","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Grundy, IL","ef":"EF0","start":13200,"end":13260,"coords":[[-88.42,41.37],[-88.4185,41.3709]],"lengthMi":0.1,"widthYd":10.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"IL","geometry":"point","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Bradley\u2013Polk, TN","ef":"EF3","start":16500,"end":17803,"coords":[[-84.92,35.1],[-84.67,35.25]],"lengthMi":18.1,"widthYd":350.0,"inj":100,"fat":1,"state":"TN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"McLean, IL","ef":"EF0","start":16620,"end":16680,"coords":[[-89.03,40.58],[-89.0285,40.5809]],"lengthMi":0.1,"widthYd":10.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"IL","geometry":"point","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Perry\u2013Washington, IN","ef":"EF5","start":17400,"end":22296,"coords":[[-86.75,38.07],[-85.7,38.63]],"lengthMi":68.0,"widthYd":0.0,"inj":86,"fat":6,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Xenia, OH","ef":"EF5","start":18000,"end":20254,"coords":[[-84.05,39.63],[-83.6,39.92]],"lengthMi":31.3,"widthYd":533.0,"inj":1150,"fat":36,"state":"OH","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Lawrence\u2013Jennings, IN","ef":"EF3","start":18000,"end":20578,"coords":[[-86.3,38.77],[-85.77,39.12]],"lengthMi":35.8,"widthYd":177.0,"inj":26,"fat":1,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Shelby\u2013Hancock, IN","ef":"EF3","start":18900,"end":20390,"coords":[[-85.87,39.58],[-85.67,39.85]],"lengthMi":20.7,"widthYd":440.0,"inj":25,"fat":1,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Hancock\u2013Henry, IN","ef":"EF4","start":19800,"end":21161,"coords":[[-85.65,39.75],[-85.45,39.98]],"lengthMi":18.9,"widthYd":0.0,"inj":17,"fat":0,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Bartholomew\u2013Franklin, IN","ef":"EF4","start":19860,"end":22423,"coords":[[-85.72,39.13],[-85.18,39.47]],"lengthMi":35.6,"widthYd":1200.0,"inj":17,"fat":4,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Clark\u2013Ripley, IN","ef":"EF4","start":20940,"end":23503,"coords":[[-85.60386,38.67568],[-85.70823,38.62206],[-85.86891,38.55765],[-85.94719,38.49534],[-86.0749,38.41576],[-86.21635,38.33501],[-86.27952,38.30269],[-86.49376,38.19592],[-86.7643,38.06197]],"lengthMi":35.6,"widthYd":700.0,"inj":190,"fat":11,"state":"IN","geometry":"surveyed","timing":"estimated","comments":"Grazulis narrative:  Moved east-northeast and northeast from three miles south of Huffman, passing southeast of Branchville, north of Sulphur Springs and Pilot Knob, south of Sulphur and Curby, across the southeast part of DePauw, hitting two miles east of Palmyra, passing through Martinsburg, crossing the southeast half of Daisy Hill, passing between Bunker Hill and New Liberty, and ending two miles north of IN 160.  This tornado immediately killed a woman as it destroyed her mobile home.  As the tornado passed along southeast of Branchville it killed again.  Two people, riding in a school bus, saw the tornado and took shelter in a nearby ditch.  The bus was thrown fifty feet into the ditch, crushing the couple and killing the woman.  Moving across Crawford County, the tornado widened to over a mile, missing many small communities and levelling several farms.  In Harrison County the tornado killed a woman in her mobile home in southeast Depauw.  Another woman was killed in her home two miles east of Palmyra.  In the southeastern corner of Washington County the tornado struck the town of Martinsburg, destroying 38 of the town's 48 homes.  Homes in the Daisy Hill area were completely swept away.","wfo":"LMK"},{"name":"Brandenburg, KY","ef":"EF5","start":21000,"end":23304,"coords":[[-86.52881,37.73445],[-86.29123,37.90911],[-86.16695,38.00115],[-86.10034,38.05686]],"lengthMi":32.0,"widthYd":800.0,"inj":270,"fat":31,"state":"KY","geometry":"surveyed","timing":"estimated","comments":"Grazulis narrative:  Touching down five miles southwest of Hardinsburg, Breckinridge County, the tornado passed along the northern edge of that town, with F3 damage to homes.  Thirteen people were injured and 35 homes were destroyed as the funnel moved to the northeast across Breckinridge County and into Meade County.  The tornado gradually enlarged and intensified as it approached Brandenburg.  The funnel devastated that town and crossed the Ohio River into Harrison County, Indiana.  At Brandenburg 128 homes were completely destroyed, many of them levelled and swept away.  Thirty businesses were destroyed and damage totalled over ten million dollars.  There were 28 deaths in the Brandenburg area.  The F4 damage occurred from north of Irvington, into Indiana.","wfo":"LMK"},{"name":"Henry\u2013Jay, IN","ef":"EF4","start":21900,"end":23196,"coords":[[-85.27,40.05],[-85.03,40.32]],"lengthMi":18.0,"widthYd":1400.0,"inj":12,"fat":1,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Jefferson\u2013Dearborn, IN","ef":"EF4","start":22200,"end":24151,"coords":[[-85.27,38.77],[-84.9,39.05]],"lengthMi":27.1,"widthYd":1133.0,"inj":104,"fat":0,"state":"IN","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated"},{"name":"Cla